{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The compatibility claim fails because SRC_004's sequential guard-installation account requires temporal ordering of installation operations to explain the 3-of-26 distribution, while SRC_005's registry-semantics mechanism (entries constrained only under a detectable guard) is atemporal and state-based. If the test merely constrains entries installed under a detectable guard regardless of when that guard was installed (SRC_005), this contradicts the sequential dependency essential to SRC_004's explanation. The proposed refutation conditions test whether the installation-order artifact generalizes, but do not test whether the two mechanisms can simultaneously explain the same data: if the sequential order is causally necessary (SRC_004), then a static registry state (SRC_005) cannot capture the mechanism, and conversely, if the registry state is sufficient, the sequential narrative is explanatorily superfluous. Thus the mechanisms contradict rather than merely differ in description.","counterexample":["A repository where the guard installation order varies but the final registry state is identical across trials: SRC_004 predicts the 3-of-26 ratio should disappear or vary with order, while SRC_005 predicts it remains constant whenever the same entries are under the detectable guard, yielding opposite predictions for the same observation.","A system where the identical set of entries is installed under a detectable guard in all cases, but the installation sequence differs: if the ratio remains 3-of-26, SRC_004 is refuted (sequence irrelevant); if it changes, SRC_005 is refuted (state insufficient)."],"premise":"SRC_004 explains the 3-of-26 result via 'sequential guard-installation account' where temporal installation order is causally essential; SRC_005 explains via 'registry-semantics mechanism' where the test constrains only entries under a detectable guard, which is a state-based condition independent of installation sequence.","target":"242b26217498f0110687e001ab998f29134e6cdb091c139b75f2871fdf3d385a"}]}